 `DM_FOLIAGE=off` (the Mac settings' Grass and ground cover row, on by default) turns the game's foliage module off at its source: grass, ferns, clover, the ivy on walls and the moss fuzz on logs. The stub in [`patches.py`](patches.py) (`foliage`, placed by the fingerprint of the module's per-frame calc, `main+0x2c00a40` on v131072) sets the module's own grass and forest disables (+0x141 / +0x142, which its timelines use) and the four per-type hide bits of its debug word (+0x2b1) every frame while state page +0x300 is 1, so the game's own checks skip the foliage draws, the per-type calc and the FoliageShader compute. Cuttable grass and bushes are actors drawn as models and stay. Brad Norman measured it on TVPort (brad-n/TVPort 8609a1cb, MIT) on a Mac mini M2 Pro: the foliage encoders came to about 3.5 ms of GPU a frame (balcony, Link's house) and 0.02 ms with the option, and graphics memory fell about 85 MB (Link's house 1346 → 1256 MB). The state offset differs from TVPort's (+0xb0 there), because upstream's wide-screen stubs use +0xa0 / +0xa4.
 
+Two more of the game's own detail knobs come from the same TVPort work (brad-n/TVPort ba9cf51e, MIT), as stubs of the frame step rule placed by function fingerprints: `DM_MODEL_LOD=<factor>` (the Model detail row; state page +0x304, a float) divides the model scene's size on screen and start distance coefficient by the factor in the three inlined level choices of the model scene calc (`main+0x7bb80`) and the module's level function (`main+0x31d48b0`, `main+0x31d4d80`), and `DM_SHADOW_CASCADES=1|2` (the Shadow range row; +0x308) lowers DepthShadowCascadeNum0 as gsys ModelSceneConfigParam loads (`main+0x35667c0`). On a Mac mini at TV-like settings a factor of 4 took 3.3 ms of 11.8 off the Great Deku Tree's dialogue and 1.2 to 1.5 ms off the balcony; one cascade took the shadow passes from 0.3 to 0.1 ms. TVPort's `DM_AB_STATE` measurement switch was not taken.
+
 ## Memory
 
 - Loading the same v131072 save into Kokiri Forest outside Link's house peaked at 9.777 GiB of macOS physical footprint on `f76fe0c1` and 9.793 GiB on `de348580` (+16 MiB, +0.16%). Both runs on the 48 GB M4 Pro MacBook Pro (macOS 27.2.1) used the warmed system Metal cache, the same route shader image with conservative uniform-buffer defaults, and frames 2000–3100. Pipeline archives, prewarm and shader prefetch were off. Other shader compiles were active on the Mac in both runs. A second fixed-build run peaked at 9.863 GiB. The matched difference is smaller than that run-to-run spread, so the change in peak footprint is inconclusive for this load. [PR #2714](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2714)
