 On by default, shown for games whose build has the stub (The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time). Off: the game's grass, ferns, clover, the ivy on walls and the moss on logs are not drawn, calculated or computed, which saves about 3.5 ms of GPU a frame and about 85 MB of graphics memory on a Mac mini M2 Pro. Grass you can cut and bushes stay. Takes effect at the next game start (`DM_FOLIAGE`).
 
+### Model detail
+
+Full by default, shown for games whose build has the stubs (Ocarina of Time). Lower (2) and Lowest (4) make the game pick its simpler models as if each were that many times farther away, which takes about 1 to 3 ms of GPU a frame off the busiest scenes on a Mac mini M2 Pro (the Great Deku Tree's dialogue, Link's balcony) and little elsewhere (`DM_MODEL_LOD`).
+
+### Shadow range
+
+Full by default (Ocarina of Time: 3 cascades). 2 or 1 cascades end the sun's shadows nearer the camera and soften near shadows; the shadow passes fall from about 0.3 to 0.1 ms a frame. The game reads it when it loads its settings, so it takes effect at the next start (`DM_SHADOW_CASCADES`).
+
